      "title": "Stokes' law sets the rise velocity",
      "description": "An oil droplet rises at v = g·d²·(ρw − ρo)/(18·μ) (Stokes). Small droplets rise very slowly, so the inclined plates give each droplet only a short distance to rise before it meets a plate surface, coalesces and slides up to the oil layer. CPI separators typically remove free oil droplets down to roughly 50–60 µm; API separators ~ 150 µm.",
